## 3. PHASE 1 — PRIMARY-SOURCE DEEP RESEARCH

Research current official docs, specs, releases and repository examples. Record source URL, publisher, publication/release date where available, access date, version checked, findings, caveats and design decision affected.

### Core source candidates to verify

These are starting points, not a claim that each is automatically the right dependency. Verify current docs, versions, coverage, licenses, and applicability.

- TanStack Table: https://tanstack.com/table/latest/docs/introduction
- TanStack Table features: https://tanstack.com/table/latest/docs/guide/features
- TanStack Virtual: https://tanstack.com/virtual/latest/docs/introduction
- shadcn/ui Data Table: https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components/data-table
- shadcn/ui Table and relevant blocks: https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components/table and https://ui.shadcn.com/blocks
- WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices Guide: https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/
- WAI-ARIA Grid Pattern: https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/grid/
- WAI-ARIA Table Pattern: https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/table/
- WCAG 2.2: https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/
- React Aria Table: https://react-spectrum.adobe.com/react-aria/Table.html
- React Aria GridList and related collection patterns where relevant: https://react-spectrum.adobe.com/react-aria/
- AG Grid documentation and licensing: https://www.ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/ and https://www.ag-grid.com/license-pricing/
- MUI X Data Grid documentation/licensing: https://mui.com/x/react-data-grid/ and https://mui.com/x/introduction/licensing/
- React documentation: https://react.dev/
- TypeScript documentation: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/
- MDN URLSearchParams: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/URLSearchParams
- MDN Intl.NumberFormat: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/NumberFormat
- MDN Intl.DateTimeFormat: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/DateTimeFormat
- Playwright: https://playwright.dev/docs/intro
- Storybook testing: https://storybook.js.org/docs/writing-tests
- RFC 4180 (CSV format overview): https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4180
- OWASP CSV Injection guidance: https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/CSV_Injection

Research additional primary sources where useful, including the current official documentation for any candidate virtualizer, grid, chart, export or state-management library. Verify the official URL remains current and do not fabricate capabilities.

### Required research questions

1. What is the meaningful distinction between semantic HTML table, headless data-table state engine, accessible ARIA grid, and a fully featured enterprise data grid?
2. Which features are suitable for Moonframe-owned behavior, which should be delegated to a headless engine, and which require a separately licensed/optional engine?
3. When is TanStack Table sufficient? When is virtualization needed? What does it not provide by itself?
4. When is an ARIA grid warranted over a semantic table, and what accessibility complexity follows?
5. What are the trade-offs of building on TanStack Table, React Aria, AG Grid, MUI X Data Grid, or other credible alternatives?
6. Which providers have feature limitations or paid-tier requirements? Verify current licensing, feature matrices and redistribution implications.
7. How should client-side and server-side filtering, sorting, pagination, grouping and selection differ in their contracts?
8. How should filter definitions serialize to URL parameters and/or saved views? What should never be stored in the URL?
9. How should row identity and selection remain stable across sorting, filtering, pagination, refresh and virtualized rendering?
10. What are accessibility requirements and known pitfalls for sorting headers, multi-select, row selection, keyboard navigation, column menus, inline editing, sticky columns and virtualized rows?
11. How should exports handle localization, large files, background-job status, permission boundaries and CSV formula injection risks?
12. How should tables reflow or degrade on mobile without simply hiding important data?
13. What are appropriate testing layers for this system, including realistic large datasets and deterministic visual regression?
14. What is the minimum capable v1 and which advanced capabilities should remain optional/future?

### Research method

- Compare at least three credible implementation approaches for the core data-table foundation.
- Build a weighted decision matrix with criteria, weights, scores, evidence, confidence, and caveats. Do not use unexplained numeric scores.
- Separate observed fact from design judgment and recommendation.
- Include the cost of migration, accessibility burden, performance risk, styling freedom, API stability and vendor lock-in.
- If a capability is unclear or source docs disagree, record uncertainty and use a small future spike as the resolution task. Do not silently guess.
- Do not treat a vendor marketing page as equivalent to detailed API docs or licensing terms.
- Keep a research log, e.g. `docs/research/advanced-data-workspace-research-log.md`, or extend an existing authoritative research log.

